## 🛠️ Command Line Interface (CLI)

The package includes both `swarm-protocol` (Node.js) and `swarm-protocol-py` (Python) executable binaries.

```bash
# Initialize swarm bus directory
swarm-protocol init

# Acquire a resource claim
swarm-protocol claim src/controllers --agent codex-cli --mode exclusive --duration 45000

# Send a heartbeat to extend active claim
swarm-protocol heartbeat <claim_id> --agent codex-cli

# Check swarm status, active claims, and recent bus events
swarm-protocol status

# Send an Envelope v2 message
swarm-protocol send --from codex-cli --to claude-code --topic task.handoff --payload '{"files":["api.ts"]}'

# Broadcast message to all registered agents
swarm-protocol broadcast --from codex-cli --topic sync.schema --payload '{"version":"v2"}'

# Receive unread messages
swarm-protocol receive --agent claude-code --ack

# Reap expired leases
swarm-protocol reap

# Two-Seat Command Studio Mission Lifecycle
swarm-protocol two-seat init --mission feat-payments --owner codex-cli --controller claude-code --checkpoint "Started payment API"
swarm-protocol two-seat handover --mission feat-payments --from codex-cli --to claude-code --next "Implement React payment form"
swarm-protocol two-seat status --mission feat-payments
```

---

## 🏛️ Two-Seat Command Studio Governance

The **Two-Seat Command Studio Model** provides high-safety multi-agent orchestration:

```
[Two-Seat Architecture]
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                        MISSION CONTRACT                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  1. Mission Owner (Current Writer / Outcome Driver)                |
|     - Directs task sequence and writes terminal closeouts         |
|     - Holds monotonic fencing generation token                    |
|                                                                   |
|  2. Studio Controller (Independent Observer / Safety Sentinel)    |
|     - Monitors health, trace verification, and proof gates        |
|     - Prohibited from countermanding or mutating owner's scope    |
|     - Can execute emergency recovery ONLY upon owner lease loss   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Safety Invariants

1. **One Authority Owner**: Exactly one seat holds mission authority at any given time.
2. **Observation is Active-Active; Writes are Mutual Exclusion**: Both seats may inspect and reason concurrently, but write scopes are guarded by monotonic fencing generations.
3. **Controller Cannot Countermand**: The controller may audit, challenge, or execute disjoint work, but cannot mutate the active owner's claimed scope.
4. **Fencing Out Stale Writers**: Any delayed or zombie worker presenting an older generation is rejected with an invariant violation.

